		    An Adventurer's Guide to Luck
			  by Robert DeLoura
			(deloura@noaapmel.gov)


This guide covers how to get it, not what to do with it.  No warrantees
expressed or implied.  :-)

Luck normally ranges from +10 to -10, with higher luck being better.
It also normally tends to move back towards zero, one point at a time, every
300 moves.  If you have the Amulet of Yendor, or your god is angry with
you (you have a negative Alignment), it only does this every 600 moves.
If you are carrying a luckstone (multiple ones don't help -- only the
first one in your inventory seems to affect it), your luck is affected
according to the following table:

		Type       Bonus     GoodLuck     BadLuck
             ----------------------------------------------
               cursed       -3       times out    holds
               uncursed     +3       times out    times out
               blessed      +3       holds        times out

In the above table, "times out" means that it tends towards zero over time,
as described in the previous paragraph.  "holds" means that this sort of luck
does not change with time while you're carrying that type of stone.  Thus,
if you have positive luck, and carry a cursed luckstone, your luck will move
back towards zero over time.  If you're carrying a blessed one, however, your
luck will not do this.  This is why blessed luckstones are so useful.

If you quaff a potion of enlightenment (or die, but the potion is probably
a better method), you'll be able to see your level of luck:

                     Intrinsic         Luck Score
                 ------------------------------------
                  extremely lucky      10 or more
                  very lucky           5 to 9
                  lucky                1 to 4
                  (not mentioned)      0
                  unlucky              -1 to -4
                  very unlucky         -5 to -9
                  extremely unlucky    -10 or less

You start the game with an extra point of luck during the full moon, and
one less point of luck if it's Friday the 13th.



THROWING GEMS AT UNICORNS
-------------------------

Throwing gems to a unicorn is a well-known way to get luck.  You get luck
according to the following table.  "Real gem" means the gem is a real gem,
not a worthless piece of glass.  "Identified" means you've read an identify
scroll on it to find out what kind of gem it is.  "Named" means you used some
other means (engraving it on the floor to see whether it said you 'wrote in
the dust' or 'engraved in the floor' with your gem) of determining whether it
was real or not (actually, the game just checks whether you've named it or
not).  "Co-aligned" means the unicorn matches your alignment (white=lawful,
grey=neutral, black=chaotic).  "Luck" is the amount of luck you get out of the
gem.  "How" is the adverb used to describe how the unicorn accepts your gift.
(Throwing any gem at a unicorn will make it peaceful, by the way.)

  Identified      Named        Real gem   Co-aligned   |   Luck       How?
-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------
     Yes           ---           Yes         Yes       |    +5     gratefully
     Yes           ---           Yes         No        | +3 to -3  hesitatingly
     Yes           ---           No          ---       |     0     (refuses)
-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------
     No            Yes           Yes         Yes       |    +2     gratefully
     No            Yes           Yes         No        | +1 to -1  hesitatingly
     No            Yes           No          ---       |     0     (refuses)
-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------
     No            No            Yes         Yes       |    +1     gratefully
     No            No            Yes         No        | +1 to -1  hesitatingly
     No            No            No          ---       |     0     graciously



RELIGION (#offering and #praying)
---------------------------------

Sacrificing (#offering to your god at an altar) is also a good way to improve
your luck.  There is a variable gain depending on traits of the monster.  Here
is a list of some of the messages you get after sacrificing, and what they
mean in terms of your luck. (not counting the variable gain)

   Your god seems "slightly mollified"             If luck negative, goes up 1.
   Your god seems "mollified"                      If luck negative, is now 0.
   You have a "hopeful feeling"                    If luck negative, goes up 1.
   You have a "feeling of reconciliation"          If luck negative, is now 0.
   You "see a 4-leaf clover at your feet"          You gained at least 1 luck.

If you pray on an altar of another alignment, -3 luck.

If you desecrate (kick, dig, etc) another alignment's altar, -1 luck.

If you #offer and convert an altar to your alignment, +1 luck.
If you #offer and FAIL to convert an altar to your alignment, -1 luck.

If you perform a human sacrifice and aren't Chaotic, -5 luck.
If you perform a human sacrifice and ARE Chaotic, +2 luck.

If you change your alignment by sacrificing at an emey altar, -3 luck.
If you try to do this, but fail, then -5 luck.

If you #offer an unidentified fake Amulet of Yendor, -1 luck.
If you identified it first, then -3 luck.

If you #pray and "a golden glow surrounds you", if luck negative, it's now 0.



MISCELLANEOUS
-------------

If you kill a co-aligned unicorn, -5 luck.
If you kill a tame creature, -1 luck.
If you kill a peaceful creature, 50% chance of -1 luck.
If you aren't Chaotic, and kill an '@' type that is sometimes peaceful (such
  as a shopkeeper) and isn't a character class, then -2 luck.  [And you also
  lose your Intrinsic Telepathy if you had it.]
If you break a mirror (throwing it or hitting a monster with it), -2 luck.
If you sit on a throne and "feel your luck is changing", +1 luck.
If you attack a blinded floating eye, 1-in-500 chance of -1 luck.
  (Seriously.  I'm not joking.)





